  "question": {
    "text": "The acceleration due to gravity is found up to an accuracy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>%</mo></math> on a planet. The energy supplied to a simple pendulum of known mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> to undertake oscillations of time period <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> is being estimated. If time period is measured to an accuracy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>%</mo></math>, the accuracy to which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> is known as ________<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "14",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>l</mi><mi>g</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi></mfrac><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mtext>Therefore</mtext><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mi>E</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>",
